From 37fafc9eb74cba4ad125a1faf7340a15ab094a23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:57:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/16] x86/mic: KNC vector-unit (VPU) state handling

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6. KNC has no SSE and no XSAVE; its 512-bit
vector registers, mask registers and VXCSR are saved and restored by
hand next to the fxsave x87 state, in the xstate layout so the signal
frame and the ptrace NT_X86_XSTATE regset carry them:
 - fpu/types.h: struct vpustate in xregs_state, XFEATURE_MASK_ZMM in
   the MPX slot; uapi sigcontext.h: struct _vpustate in _xstate.
 - fpu/core.c, xstate.h: save = fxsave + save_init_vpu(), restore =
   fxrstor + VPU reload (os_xrstor{,_safe} EARLYMIC versions); the
   mask registers are reloaded on every context switch (kmov ignores
   CR0.TS).
 - MXCSR.DUE errata: fxsave to the user sigframe forces DUE
   (legacy.h); VXCSR_DEFAULT instead of 0x1f80 (MBZ on KNC).
 - fpu/init.c: no CR4.OSFXSR/OSXMMEXCPT; fpu/xstate.c: no XSAVE, so
   fpu__init_system_xstate() sets the feature mask and sizes by hand.
 - mic_ni.h: the VPU save/restore/mask helpers; no emms (no MMX).

Adaptations for 6.18: rebuilt on the 6.x FPU core (struct fpstate,
fpu_kernel_cfg/fpu_user_cfg, fpstate_init_user(), x86_task_fpu(),
kernel/fpu/{internal,legacy,xstate}.h after the 5.16 split of
asm/fpu/internal.h). init_fpstate is __ro_after_init since 5.14: the
MK1OM LDVXCSR macro normalizes VXCSR in a register and loads from the
stack. 6.15 dropped the FPU state of kernel threads: the idle task is
no longer reset from the KNC xstate init. The VPU helpers emit
relative (_ASM_EXTABLE) exception-table entries; the 2.6-era 16-byte
absolute ones corrupted the sorted table (#GP storm from the
CSTAR/SYSENTER wrmsrl_safe fixups).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
